{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355048-infrastructure-protection","id":1355048,"title":"Infrastructure Protection","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-15T13:56:37-08:00","id":1355048,"title":"Infrastructure Protection","content":"I'd like to use a network of weather monitoring stations as Infrastructure. The idea is that small, automated stations might be hackable Infrastructure with a small pool of Aether available, larger automated stations might have more, while still larger staffed stations would have more Aether and more access to GM information but more dangerous protection. <br /> <br /> However, I am not sure how such systems might be protected. Certainly the small stations would not have an angel manning them, but they wouldn't be unprotected. The larger stations might have an Angel on staff, but I am not sure what level of security would be appropriate. What have you used in your campaigns to protect Infrastructure?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T11:15:03-08:00","id":1355216,"title":"","content":"I would look to some of the source material. Use the Clockwork servitors. Maybe some normal human agents that are actually cultists. Defensive Infrastructure doesn't have to be an angel. As it says in DtD core rulebook (page 62), the G-M is more likely to employ a sniper on a roof than a nightmarish creature.<br /> <br /> Don't limit Infrastructure to just some kind of machine or cryptid. It can be anything that the G-M thinks might be useful for a task.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14512-ghostdriver","name":"Ghostdriver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14512_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T11:16:20-08:00","id":1355217,"title":"","content":"I made a form of Command + Control Infrastructure in my game that is a weather station. I made it with the following defenses:<ul><li>Environmental - Weather Station is on top of a mountain with only one access road to get to.</li> <li>Cryptids - The mountain has a small population of Yeti that act as defense against anyone trying to climb the mountain.</li> <li>Security System - The Facility has cameras and security doors as basic mundane protection.</li> <li>Sleeper Agents - Some of the mortals who work on the station are actually Sleeper Agents whose trigger can be used when the Facility is breached.</li> <li>Stigmatics - Some of the Security team are stigmatics who are trained in preventing Demon incursion.</li> <li>Angel - A Guardian Angel designed to protect the system. Oversees most of the security team.</li> </ul>While mine was a big piece of Infrastructure, you could use parts of this to secure your smaller Infrastructure. Hopefully this gave you some ideas on what you might like to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T12:43:05-08:00","id":1355236,"title":"","content":"I might even go with don't, at least at first, it sounds like a setup that might be able to have some redundancy if the whole weather network in X region is being used. So have the small one aren't that well defended because some losses means less information is coming in, but might be a few alarms (even mostly mundane that trigger) and possibly routines that if the information stops flowing triggers angels to investigate and repair. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/711-mcgonigle","name":"mcgonigle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T16:27:21-08:00","id":1355290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mcgonigle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355048-infrastructure-protection?p=1355236#post1355236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might even go with don't, at least at first, it sounds like a setup that might be able to have some redundancy if the whole weather network in X region is being used. So have the small one aren't that well defended because some losses means less information is coming in, but might be a few alarms (even mostly mundane that trigger) and possibly routines that if the information stops flowing triggers angels to investigate and repair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good idea. I'll probably start with the minor ones undefended. After a few incursions the minor ones might have minor protection.<br /> <br /> The middling ones will have some sort of servitor at first, or a human nearby. Bigger payoff in Aether and information, but bigger risk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T06:45:37-08:00","id":1355391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355048-infrastructure-protection?p=1355290#post1355290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good idea. I'll probably start with the minor ones undefended. After a few incursions the minor ones might have minor protection.<br /> <br /> The middling ones will have some sort of servitor at first, or a human nearby. Bigger payoff in Aether and information, but bigger risk.</div> </div> </div> </div>The minor ones will probably at the very least have a Mortal Security guard. Who may be at risk of becoming a Stigmatic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}